WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.529
Brynden Tully: Other houses chose dragons,
krakens, and lions for their sigils.

00:00:05.529 --> 00:00:08.710
We Tullys took the trout.

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:14.130
That most terrifying of fish, especially when
it leaps out of the water.

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:19.999
I suppose you don't have many options when
you live in the Riverlands.

00:00:19.999 --> 00:00:22.579
Could've been worse.

00:00:22.579 --> 00:00:23.660
We could have been minnows.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:25.759
Or wheat (after all, we make a lot of it).

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:30.829
Though a land does not get as fertile as ours
just by water.

00:00:30.829 --> 00:00:36.329
The old River Kings, Storm Kings, and the
Kings of the Rock spilled blood here for thousands

00:00:36.329 --> 00:00:40.989
of years, squabbling like children over a
new toy.

00:00:40.989 --> 00:00:45.230
Until the ironborn came and spanked them with
their axes.

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:51.339
Under Harren the Black, their kingdom stretched
all the way to the Gods Eye, where they built

00:00:51.339 --> 00:00:55.680
the largest castle Westeros had ever seen.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:00.660
Maesters teach that Harren was a fool, but
he had some sense.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:05.309
If you're going to enslave and torture an
entire people, you best have thick walls to

00:01:05.309 --> 00:01:06.360
hide behind.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:15.700
But the very day the last stone was laid in
Harrenhal, Aegon Targaryen landed in Westeros.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:20.860
As soon as he saw Aegon's host on the horizon,
my ancestor Edmyn led the mass desertion of

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:23.590
Riverlords to Aegon's side.

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:25.930
I doubt Harren even noticed.

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:32.009
The problem with huge castles is they blind
you to what's outside, both by their size

00:01:32.009 --> 00:01:35.800
and the arrogance they inspire.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:38.260
Not that the ironborn ever lacked for that.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:42.780
They take pride in their ignorance of every
trapping of civilization.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:48.411
Though any baker could have told them that
fire turns stone walls into an oven.

00:01:48.411 --> 00:01:56.110
And so Harren the Black finally lived up to
his name, and the Riverlords swept the ironborn

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:57.600
back to the sea.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:03.030
In return for Edmyn's service, House Tully
was made Aegon's new Lord Paramount of the

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:07.899
Trident, and all of the other lords had to
swear us fealty.

00:02:07.899 --> 00:02:10.509
But old habits die hard.

00:02:10.509 --> 00:02:15.819
The Riverlands are and always have been the
middle child of Westeros, caught up in every

00:02:15.819 --> 00:02:18.950
fart from one lord at another.

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:25.420
My ancestors knew that for the Tullys to survive,
alliances must be made.

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:31.590
Our trout has swum up so many rivers over
the centuries and leapt onto so many plates

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:35.800
that it's a wonder half of the realm's sigils
do not have fins by now.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:42.459
Thus every Tully child is taught "Family,
Duty, Honor," the Tully words.

00:02:42.459 --> 00:02:49.930
Euron Greyjoy: Harren of House Hoare inherited
a kingdom that stretched from the Iron Islands

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:51.650
to the Trident.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:56.450
Too great a kingdom to rule from a castle
as as Pyke.

00:02:56.450 --> 00:03:02.959
For forty years, his ironborn plundered the
Riverlands for stone, timber, and slaves to

00:03:02.959 --> 00:03:05.099
build a seat worthy of him.

00:03:05.099 --> 00:03:13.030
Legend has it that masons laid the final stone
in Harrenhal on the very day that Aegon landed

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:14.599
in Westeros.

00:03:14.599 --> 00:03:17.069
Could've been a divine omen.

00:03:17.069 --> 00:03:22.959
Could've been the masons wanted to go off
before the dragons got there.

00:03:22.959 --> 00:03:25.780
They weren't the only ones.

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:31.470
At Aegon's approach, Harren'sriverlords revolted,
led by House Tully.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:34.769
I doubt Harren noticed.

00:03:34.769 --> 00:03:38.260
Harrenhal could repel an army of a million
men.

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:43.010
No ladder could summit its walls, and ram
could shatter them.

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:46.459
The castle was as impregnable as an old maid's.

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:53.629
Harren shut his gates around himself, his
sons and his ironborn, and waited for Aegon's

00:03:53.629 --> 00:03:56.830
army to drain back into the muck.

00:03:56.830 --> 00:04:01.849
When Aegon finally saw the monstrous castle,
he asked for parley.

00:04:01.849 --> 00:04:04.510
Harren granted it.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:08.849
Valyria had been the greatest empire the world
had ever seen.

00:04:08.849 --> 00:04:12.599
Harren wanted to piss on its ashes.

00:04:12.599 --> 00:04:18.540
Viserys Targaryen: (as Aegon) "Yield now,
and you may remain Lord of the Iron Islands.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:23.410
Yield now, and your sons will live to rule
after you.

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:26.700
You see my army outside your walls.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:27.970
You see my dragons."

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:33.380
Euron: (as Harren) "What is outside my walls
is of no concern.

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:35.130
Those walls are strong and thick."

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:37.230
Viserys: (as Aegon) "Dragons fly."

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:41.540
Euron: (as Harren) "But stone doesn't burn."

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:46.010
Viserys: (as Aegon) "When the sun sets, your
line shall end."

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:51.180
Euron: Harren spat and returned to his castle.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:56.260
Once inside, he promised lands, riches, and
Tully's daughters to whoever could bring down

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:58.700
Aegon or his dragon.

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:05.570
As the sun sank below the horizon, all Harren's
men patrolled the battlements, hearing wings

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:08.550
in every gust of wind.

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:13.340
But the moon rose and sank, and no dragon
appeared.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:19.050
Viserys: While the ironborn were ringing the
battlements, Aegon drove his dragon Balerion

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:23.580
higher and higher in the night sky, so that
even the great castle of Harrenhal looked

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:25.630
like an anthill below them.

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:30.690
Then they plunged straight into the castle,
well inside the guarded walls.

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:34.880
The five towers of Harrenhal reached towards
Aegon like a hand.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:38.650
Balerion opened his mouth and bathed all the
fingers in flame.

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:41.690
Euron: Harren was right.

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:47.760
Stone doesn't burn, but men do, even when
they're ironborn.

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:55.220
The dragon blasted my ancestors into ash that
choked the survivors when they screamed.

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:58.260
Harren's soldiers leapt from the battlements
and died.

00:05:58.260 --> 00:06:02.550
They huddled against the walls and died.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:05.190
They fled across the yard and died.

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:08.690
Harren and his sons took shelter inside the
castle.

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:19.460
The stone didn't burn, but as Balerion blasted
it with fire, it glowed white-hot.

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:26.880
The world's greatest castle became the world's
greatest oven, baking the last of House Hoare

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:28.140
within it.

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:33.930
Viserys: Outside the castle walls, the towers
of Harrenhal glowed red against the night

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:39.370
and began to twist and melt like five huge
candles, with liquid stone trickling down

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:42.100
their sides like wax.

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:46.020
The next morning, Aegon forged a new Riverlands.

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:50.870
He named the rebel Edmyn Tully as his Lord
Paramount of the Trident and had the other

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:53.970
riverlords swear him fealty as their new liege.

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:58.560
For centuries, House Hoare had terrorized
the Riverlands.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:04.630
Under House Tully, the Riverlands would, at
last, return to peace and prosperity.

00:07:04.630 --> 00:07:09.570
After the castle cooled enough to allow men
inside, Aegon ventured into the ruin he had

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:11.450
made of Harrenhal.

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:17.740
He saw the ashen bodies, the scorched stone,
and the mangled and melted swords of his former

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:18.960
enemies.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:24.280
To his men's confusion, he ordered these useless
swords collected and sent to his Aegonfort.

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:30.540
Brynden Tully: Men have fought over the Riverlands
since the Dawn Age, but that's to be expected

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:33.080
of things that rest below the Neck.

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:37.350
Doesn't help that the Riverlands are between
everything and everything else.

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:45.360
The Westerlands' gold, the Reach's grain,
the Vale's rock and the North's... snow?

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:51.740
House Mudd once ruled as the Kings of the
Rivers and Hills, but after a thousand years,

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:57.120
their line was exhausted and fell to the Storm
Kings, who fell to the ironborn.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:02.610
I suppose after years of drowning at sea,
our rivers looked pretty attractive to that

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:04.180
race of pirates.

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:11.120
Never mind that their monstrous castle, Harrenhal,
was too large to staff and garrison.

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:15.140
It turned out the ironborn would not be there
long enough to bother.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:21.640
Aegon Targaryen landed to our south and, as
had many before him, liked the look of the

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:22.800
Riverlands.

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:27.470
My ancestor Edmyn Tully led the desertion
of Riverlords to his cause and was rewarded

00:08:27.470 --> 00:08:31.170
by getting to watch King Harren burn in his
own tower.

00:08:31.170 --> 00:08:35.990
Unfortunately, that's not all Edmyn got.

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:41.880
House Tully was named the Lord Paramount of
the Trident, which means we had to keep in

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:48.200
line all those lords who hadn't governed themselves
for thousands of years.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:54.590
We were now responsible for aiding the Mallisters
at Seagard against the pouting ironborn, whenever

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:56.360
they got cheeky.

00:08:56.360 --> 00:09:02.640
For settling Harrenhal on families stupid
enough to think its curse would skip them,

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:05.310
after devouring all previous families.

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:11.170
For keeping the Blackwoods and Brackens from
wiping each other out, and giving us two more

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:13.480
castles to deal with.

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:18.020
For keeping the Freys in their place and out
of others' pockets.

00:09:18.020 --> 00:09:24.190
For marrying off our sons and daughters wisely
enough so that we didn't follow House Mudd

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:28.900
into, well, the mud.

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:35.770
Yet under the Targaryens, the Riverlands knew
a peace we hadn't had for centuries, if ever.

00:09:35.770 --> 00:09:44.320
But like all good things, sooner or later,
it all goes to . And our had a name.

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:47.640
Aerys Targaryen.

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:52.020
Westeros has had its share of Mad Kings, but
usually, they had the sense not to bully more

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:54.470
than one powerful house at a time.

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:58.130
Aerys soon blundered into a triple alliance.

00:09:58.130 --> 00:10:02.250
The North, the Stormlands, and the Vale rose
against him.

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:06.090
But of course, where do you think most of
the blood was spilled?

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:10.310
My brother Hoster guaranteed the answer to
that with the marriage of my niece to Eddard

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:12.240
Stark, the Warden of the North.

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:15.340
At least Hoster didn't send her to Robert.

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:21.800
So, the Riverlands joined the war against
the Mad King; and it was on one of our rivers

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:27.220
that Prince Rhaegar died, sealing the fate
of his dynasty.

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:31.490
Robert was a great soldier and a horrible
king.

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:35.520
He died and another war started.

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:40.580
Again the armies marched, again the Riverlands
burned.

00:10:40.580 --> 00:10:45.310
If Westeros is not careful, pretty soon our
people will grow some sense and abandon this

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:49.790
place for a safer realm, like the Dothraki
Sea.

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:53.080
I joke, of course.

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:57.580
The Riverlands are our home and gods help
us, we love it.

00:10:57.580 --> 00:11:06.040
Still, as they say, "the king eats and the
hand takes the ." The same is true of the

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:12.399
Riverlands – the Seven Kingdoms piss and
the Riverlands change clothes.

